message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Named AgNP observation-channel scores as forcing provenance under evidence gates"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  When a named papaya AgNP observation channel produces scores that are
  barred from Theta, which of those scores, if any, may be admitted only as
  provenance of a protocol-constant tip-ODE forcing without gate bypass or
  soft-prior leakage? One record may. It is the class-B summary of C_amyl
  from Thesis #8, admitted once as provenance of u_tip = 1. The rank, the
  leading eigenvalue, the condition, and K_c are not copied. Companion
  channels are refused. The SHA-256 of kinetic Theta remains the Thesis #19
  digest 1ace2bb9eed19f85046f25ab690076d0d5920cf19219ddb362c775be9f41d0e8.
  Not a dose. Not a medical device. No document DOI.
keywords:
  - silver nanoparticle
  - observation channel
  - alpha-amylase map
  - forcing provenance
  - evidence gate
  - protocol-constant input
  - kinetic digest
  - research-only
